WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.696
Priya: Approve one canary cohort for this window. The staged rollout starts with one partition.

2
00:00:06.696 --> 00:00:13.440
Lukas: Drain the old worker before assigning ownership. Two workers mustn't process the same partition.

3
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:20.903
Raj: Just to confirm, the lease transfers once, right? I'll verify no overlapping writer remains.

4
00:00:20.903 --> 00:00:28.271
Anika: Okay, keep an eye on reconciliation lag. Maybe the first batch warms connections slowly.

5
00:00:28.271 --> 00:00:36.575
Hannah: The smoke test uses this production partition. Compare output counts with its expected inventory.

6
00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:42.647
Raj: The new worker holds the sole lease. Token refresh and the initial batch pass.

7
00:00:42.647 --> 00:00:50.687
Lukas: State the rollback trigger before further batches. Duplicates or reconciliation mismatches mean immediate pause.

8
00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:58.222
Priya: Agreed, pause and evaluate before reverting ownership. Don't start old workers beside new ones.

9
00:00:58.222 --> 00:01:07.462
Hannah: First-batch counts and signatures match expectations. We'll inspect another full token-refresh cycle.

10
00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:15.190
Anika: I'll own that observation before expansion approval. Healthy startup alone doesn't cover steady-state behavior.

